<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/living-room.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/living-room-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/living-room.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Idaho appraisal FAQ</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers</p><h1>Idaho Insurance Appraisal Questions, Answered</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions Idaho property owners ask most about appraisal, grouped by topic: how it works, costs and timing, Idaho specifics and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-w" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Topics"><p class="toc-t">Jump to a topic</p><ul><li><a href="#faq-0">How appraisal works</a></li><li><a href="#faq-1">Costs and timing</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Idaho specifics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="faq-0">How appraisal works</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most clauses, either the policyholder or the insurer can make a written demand once the two sides disagree on the amount of loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal decide coverage?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally no. Appraisal decides the amount of loss. Whether something is covered is a separate question that may require an attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is the appraisal award binding?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The award is generally binding on the amount of loss once two of the three panel members sign it, subject to the policy’s terms and limited legal challenges.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Costs and timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does appraisal cost?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Each side pays its own appraiser and usually half of the umpire’s fee. Fee arrangements vary, so get yours in writing before work begins.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many residential appraisals finish within two to three months after both appraisers are named. Larger or more complex claims take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a minimum claim size for appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No legal minimum, but fees can absorb a small gap. Our claim gap estimator shows whether the numbers make sense.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Idaho specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance companies in Idaho?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Idaho Department of Insurance, based in Boise. It licenses insurers and accepts consumer complaints about claim handling.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Idaho have a FAIR plan?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Idaho doesn’t operate a FAIR plan or a state wind pool like some coastal states. Owners who can’t find standard coverage, such as in high wildfire-risk areas, often turn to surplus lines insurers.</p></div></details><details><summary>What weather causes the most Idaho property claims?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Hail, wind and microbursts, winter freezes, heavy snow and wildfire all generate significant claims. The mix varies by region, from the Panhandle to the Upper Snake River Plain.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is earthquake damage covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Standard homeowners policies typically exclude earth movement. Earthquake coverage is usually a separate endorsement or policy. Idaho has had notable quakes, including the 1983 Borah Peak and 2020 Stanley earthquakes.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you work for the insurance company?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When we’re your appraiser, we’re retained by you. When we serve as an umpire, we’re neutral and represent neither side.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. We provide appraisal, estimate review and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and we don’t give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you serve my area?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>We serve all 44 Idaho counties, with regular work in the Treasure Valley, Eastern Idaho, the Magic Valley, North Idaho and the Wood River Valley.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I have ready before calling?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page, the insurer’s full estimate, any letters from the insurer, your photos and any contractor estimate.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>A short call tells you whether appraisal fits your claim, or whether something else would serve you better.</p><a class="big-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-y full" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm MT</small></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Resources</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/how-the-appraisal-clause-works/">How the appraisal clause works<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/idaho-appraisal-questions/" aria-current="page">Idaho appraisal FAQ<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms-defined/">Claim terms defined<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-know-how/">Appraisal know-how guides<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We’re glad to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-w" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
